---
title: Focaccia
servings: 6
yield: 1 focaccia, 26 x 20 cm
tags: [italian, vegan]
cuisine: italian
source: Focaccia recipe (it's incredible) by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/focaccia/
---

== Dough ==

Boil the @potato{1/2}(large, floury, in 2.5 cm chunks) ~{10%minutes} to 15
minutes, until tender. Drain, mash smooth and let it cool. Measure out 125 g.

In a #large bowl{}, mix the @bread flour{1.67%cup}, @granulated sugar{4%tsp},
@kosher salt{1.25%tsp} and @instant yeast{1%tsp}.

Add the @extra virgin olive oil{1.5%tbsp} and @water{3/4%cup}(very warm, about 40°C/104°F)
and mix until no dry flour is left. It will be sticky; add a
spoonful more water only if it looks dry.

Work in the 125 g of mashed potato and gather the dough into a rough ball.
Cover and leave somewhere warm, about 25°C, ~{30%minutes}, until it has grown
by half or doubled.

Oil a second bowl with @extra virgin olive oil{2%tsp}. Move the dough into it,
fold the edges into the middle six times, turn it into a ball, cover and leave
~{30%minutes} more.

== Garlic and rosemary topping ==

Cut the @garlic{5%cloves} into fine batons. Warm them in a #small saucepan{}
with @extra virgin olive oil{3/4%cup} over medium heat until the oil is hot,
then turn it to low and cook ~{10%minutes} without letting it sizzle. Strain
and let the garlic cool. Keep the oil for another use.

== Shape and bake ==

Spread @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp} over the base and sides of a
#rectangular baking pan{}(26.5 x 20 cm, or a 23 cm round cake pan). Tip in the
dough and stretch it to fill the pan as well as it will.

Cover and leave ~{40%minutes}, until it fills the pan and has risen by about a
quarter.

Heat the oven to 220°C (430°F; 200°C fan) for at least 15 minutes, rack in the
middle.

Rub the top with @extra virgin olive oil{2%tsp}. Press your fingers deep into
the dough about six times to dimple it. Press in the garlic and scatter the
@rosemary{2.5%tsp}(finely chopped).

Drizzle with @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp} so it pools in the dimples, and
sprinkle with @flaky sea salt{1/4%tsp}.

Bake ~{25%minutes} to 30 minutes, until deep golden on top and crusty at the
edges. Turn it out onto a #wire rack{} and rest at least ~{10%minutes} before
cutting.

> Instead of garlic and rosemary, press in squashed cherry tomatoes or pitted
> kalamata olives with a little dried oregano.
